WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }
::cue(c.colora8c7fa) { color: #a8c7fa; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Premium</c></b>
Keep the project alive: <c.colora8c7fa>ko-fi.com/not6ip</c>

2
00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:03.310
Get running, get running

3
00:00:03.550 --> 00:00:06.420
holding our flag high in the sky

4
00:00:12.730 --> 00:00:18.010
Cross this endless sea with me and search for

5
00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:21.770
a global miracle no one

6
00:00:21.820 --> 00:00:23.890
has yet been able to find

7
00:00:24.780 --> 00:00:27.920
With our hearts pounding,

8
00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:29.710
we'll just charge ahead as we please, following

9
00:00:29.710 --> 00:00:35.570
the footprints of those who pursue their dreams

10
00:00:36.370 --> 00:00:39.390
No matter how stormy the night,

11
00:00:39.390 --> 00:00:42.350
if we put our minds together,

12
00:00:42.350 --> 00:00:46.480
we'll get through it

13
00:00:46.630 --> 00:00:47.860
always

14
00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:51.550
Get running, get running

15
00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:54.490
holding our flag high in the sky

16
00:00:54.560 --> 00:00:57.090
Even though there are tears

17
00:00:57.160 --> 00:01:00.560
we don't want anyone to see

18
00:01:00.730 --> 00:01:03.450
Keep chasing, keep chasing

19
00:01:03.700 --> 00:01:06.460
the compass that leads to our dreams

20
00:01:06.570 --> 00:01:09.190
always points straight ahead

21
00:01:09.190 --> 00:01:11.340
We can't stop here

22
00:01:18.790 --> 00:01:21.450
Get running, get running,

23
00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:24.500
head past everyone else

24
00:01:24.590 --> 00:01:27.080
So long as we don't run from it,

25
00:01:27.180 --> 00:01:30.520
we can take hold of tomorrow

26
00:01:30.550 --> 00:01:33.550
Keep chasing, keep chasing

27
00:01:33.640 --> 00:01:36.470
everything we see in the moment,

28
00:01:36.520 --> 00:01:38.930
we should record it all

29
00:01:39.100 --> 00:01:41.390
in the blank slates of our minds

30
00:01:50.060 --> 00:01:55.380
<b>Monster</b>

31
00:02:03.880 --> 00:02:13.180
Showing mercy is unbecoming of a raging lion!

32
00:02:13.180 --> 00:02:14.390
Ouch!

33
00:02:16.100 --> 00:02:19.780
Taking the second rumble ball is like gambling.

34
00:02:19.780 --> 00:02:22.560
There are seven transformations in total.

35
00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:27.660
In other words, the probability of
getting Arm Point is one in seven.

36
00:02:28.710 --> 00:02:33.670
If I could get it, I could hammer
my strongest attack into him.

37
00:02:34.150 --> 00:02:37.340
That's my only chance!

38
00:02:37.640 --> 00:02:39.390
Arm Point!

39
00:02:40.070 --> 00:02:42.970
Shishi Kebab!

40
00:02:48.610 --> 00:02:50.500
For my friends...

41
00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:52.460
Arm Point!

42
00:02:54.360 --> 00:02:55.940
Arm Point!

43
00:02:59.300 --> 00:03:00.630
Wrong one!

44
00:03:00.630 --> 00:03:03.200
Wrong one! Why doesn't it come out?!

45
00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:06.870
My body is at the end of its rope.
I somehow have to get Arm Point out!

46
00:03:09.540 --> 00:03:10.500
Hm?

47
00:03:11.660 --> 00:03:13.470
Whoa!

48
00:03:13.470 --> 00:03:15.630
It's out! I didn't notice it!

49
00:03:15.630 --> 00:03:17.340
Be prepared!

50
00:03:17.340 --> 00:03:19.130
I'll put everything I have...

51
00:03:19.130 --> 00:03:20.760
into this attack!

52
00:03:21.360 --> 00:03:23.110
Cloven...

53
00:03:23.110 --> 00:03:25.390
Shishi Finger Pistol!

54
00:03:32.390 --> 00:03:36.470
If I back off now, I won't get another chance!

55
00:03:36.470 --> 00:03:37.230
Cloven...

56
00:03:38.240 --> 00:03:40.240
Iron Body: Adamantine!

57
00:03:40.740 --> 00:03:43.540
Roseo Blizzard!

58
00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:49.870
Go down!

59
00:03:49.870 --> 00:03:53.830
That was my best attack!

60
00:03:57.540 --> 00:03:59.280
Ahh...

61
00:04:04.240 --> 00:04:07.940
Ahh... splendid...!

62
00:04:07.940 --> 00:04:14.560
It was indeed a beautiful blizzard of...
cherry blossom petals.

63
00:04:16.570 --> 00:04:18.190
I can't...

64
00:04:20.110 --> 00:04:22.150
I can't...

65
00:04:23.440 --> 00:04:25.610
Did I do it?

66
00:04:32.580 --> 00:04:35.440
I can't bear it anymore!

67
00:04:35.440 --> 00:04:39.140
I will give you hell!

68
00:04:45.380 --> 00:04:47.590
Tempest Kick: Lotus!

69
00:04:51.070 --> 00:04:55.560
This is it. I no longer have the energy to fight back.

70
00:04:56.710 --> 00:04:58.110
Chopper!

71
00:04:59.040 --> 00:05:02.820
Chopper, what in the world did you do?

72
00:05:03.760 --> 00:05:06.280
I don't remember.

73
00:05:09.680 --> 00:05:13.110
"I don't remember" doesn't cut it.

74
00:05:13.110 --> 00:05:17.080
It was good that no one died, at least.

75
00:05:17.080 --> 00:05:19.870
Even while you were sleeping,

76
00:05:19.870 --> 00:05:22.750
the entire country was making
a big fuss about that night.

77
00:05:22.750 --> 00:05:25.380
How are we going to settle that?

78
00:05:25.380 --> 00:05:28.090
So I did something that terrible?

79
00:05:28.090 --> 00:05:30.770
You almost destroyed an entire village.

80
00:05:30.770 --> 00:05:33.920
It's fine that you love experiments,
just like your old man did,

81
00:05:33.920 --> 00:05:38.060
but you have to account for all possible outcomes when conducting them.

82
00:05:39.130 --> 00:05:42.020
All possible outcomes?

83
00:05:42.480 --> 00:05:46.150
Good grief. You even stir up trouble like him.

84
00:05:47.490 --> 00:05:49.650
I'm sorry, Doctorine.

85
00:05:49.650 --> 00:05:51.320
I won't do it again.

86
00:05:51.320 --> 00:05:54.790
I'll never do it again,
so please don't kick me out.

87
00:05:56.320 --> 00:06:00.290
You're such a fool. Hurry up and get better.

88
00:06:00.290 --> 00:06:01.950
I can't even go shopping.

89
00:06:04.620 --> 00:06:08.010
Vital Response!

90
00:06:08.740 --> 00:06:10.550
Hair Bind!

91
00:06:15.460 --> 00:06:18.760
Don't cry. Don't cry.

92
00:06:18.760 --> 00:06:22.110
If you do, it'll be a disgrace to your manhood.

93
00:06:22.110 --> 00:06:23.690
He's gonna kill me.

94
00:06:23.690 --> 00:06:29.730
This isn't an evening in a mountain
village where you can hear the cicadas.

95
00:06:29.730 --> 00:06:37.200
This is a journey to hell's furnace
that you knew could come.

96
00:06:37.200 --> 00:06:41.140
The leaves I took from a willow tree to give to you as a parting gift,

97
00:06:41.140 --> 00:06:44.380
hoping for your return someday,
are colored crimson!

98
00:06:44.380 --> 00:06:48.830
Take it! Now, now, now, now!

99
00:06:48.830 --> 00:06:54.850
Crimson... Song of the Willow!

100
00:06:55.780 --> 00:06:57.430
I'm gonna die.

101
00:07:00.420 --> 00:07:04.270
Robin! That's right. I can't give up!

102
00:07:08.170 --> 00:07:10.550
He slipped away from my Hair Bind!

103
00:07:10.550 --> 00:07:11.360
Rumble!

104
00:07:15.160 --> 00:07:18.950
If I'm gonna die anyway, I'll do it!

105
00:07:18.950 --> 00:07:23.630
Just please, nobody come into this room.

106
00:07:26.610 --> 00:07:29.590
I used three rumble balls.

107
00:07:29.590 --> 00:07:34.550
Then I lost consciousness and after that...

108
00:07:34.550 --> 00:07:39.060
You could say that your devil fruit
powers went out of control.

109
00:07:39.060 --> 00:07:43.520
Don't ever go down that path again, okay?

110
00:07:43.520 --> 00:07:49.490
It's too much power. It destroys
foes, friends, and even your own body.

111
00:07:49.490 --> 00:07:52.210
What you turned into was just like a real...

112
00:07:56.780 --> 00:07:58.820
monster.

113
00:08:09.440 --> 00:08:10.420
Dammit!

114
00:08:11.490 --> 00:08:16.600
I'm super this week, and yet I still
had a harder time than I thought.

115
00:08:20.160 --> 00:08:21.560
But, well...

116
00:08:23.520 --> 00:08:25.580
I got his key.

117
00:08:29.080 --> 00:08:30.940
No. 4.

118
00:08:31.440 --> 00:08:35.440
The key the swordsman and
the nose wanted was No. 2, right?

119
00:08:35.850 --> 00:08:37.680
This guy had No. 4.

120
00:08:37.680 --> 00:08:39.360
That guy had No. 3.

121
00:08:39.360 --> 00:08:41.550
And there's only one left.

122
00:08:41.550 --> 00:08:45.680
The one with the No. 2 key
is that secretary woman!

123
00:08:46.260 --> 00:08:48.500
I'd better hurry up.

124
00:08:48.500 --> 00:08:50.340
I'll go help them out!

125
00:09:13.540 --> 00:09:16.200
You guys don't have much time, right?

126
00:09:16.200 --> 00:09:19.580
I thought you weren't going to go easy on me.

127
00:09:19.580 --> 00:09:22.200
Did I hear you wrong?

128
00:09:22.200 --> 00:09:25.040
How dare you mock me?!
I won't let you get away with it!

129
00:09:25.540 --> 00:09:28.080
Then, bring it on.

130
00:09:28.080 --> 00:09:33.340
You don't have to wait. The battle
has already started, you know.

131
00:09:33.340 --> 00:09:38.970
I'm surprised that an ability user
would take a bath in front of her enemy.

132
00:09:38.970 --> 00:09:42.850
If your body is halfway submerged,
you shouldn't have full use of your powers.

133
00:09:43.350 --> 00:09:47.020
Are you saying that I'm
leaving myself wide open?

134
00:09:51.150 --> 00:09:53.780
You don't have to worry about it,

135
00:09:53.780 --> 00:09:57.030
because just like me, you can't
exert your strength, either.

136
00:09:57.030 --> 00:09:58.390
Pardon me for a bit.

137
00:10:07.080 --> 00:10:09.540
What'd you do to me?!

138
00:10:11.690 --> 00:10:17.670
Isn't solving a mystery like that one of
the true joys of fighting an ability user?

139
00:10:23.430 --> 00:10:28.100
It was definitely this woman
who put Sanji-kun in that state.

140
00:10:28.820 --> 00:10:32.730
I have to be careful. Or there's no
point in me taking his place to fight.

141
00:10:35.410 --> 00:10:38.650
The strength I lost is coming back little by little.

142
00:10:43.750 --> 00:10:48.330
I'll show you the power
of the Perfect Clima-Tact!

143
00:10:48.760 --> 00:10:52.540
You're mistaken if you think
I'm just a dainty beauty!

144
00:10:55.910 --> 00:10:57.420
I can move my legs, too!

145
00:11:02.760 --> 00:11:04.520
Here I come!

146
00:11:05.470 --> 00:11:07.220
Thunder Charge!

147
00:11:09.630 --> 00:11:11.280
Swing Arm!

148
00:11:25.720 --> 00:11:27.410
That's an amazing weapon.

149
00:11:31.610 --> 00:11:33.080
These are...

150
00:11:34.150 --> 00:11:35.790
clouds?

151
00:11:35.790 --> 00:11:38.800
There's no way I'd just lay on
the floor doing nothing, is there?

152
00:11:40.010 --> 00:11:44.800
Thunderbolt... Tempo!

153
00:11:56.130 --> 00:11:59.320
It's your own fault for acting so confident.

154
00:12:20.500 --> 00:12:22.290
That was a surprise.

155
00:12:22.290 --> 00:12:25.430
I never thought I'd be hit by lightning indoors.

156
00:12:27.180 --> 00:12:31.030
What was that thing that
guarded you from the lightning?

157
00:12:31.030 --> 00:12:33.150
It turned into bubbles and disappeared.

158
00:12:33.150 --> 00:12:36.860
You have no chance against me
unless you solve that mystery.

159
00:12:38.410 --> 00:12:40.530
I wonder if you can do it.

160
00:12:40.530 --> 00:12:43.870
It was as if soap turned into bubbles.

161
00:12:43.870 --> 00:12:46.510
You could be a soap human with Bubble Bubble Fruit powers.

162
00:12:46.510 --> 00:12:48.090
I wonder if it's something like that.

163
00:12:49.700 --> 00:12:53.430
B-But even if, for example, you figured
out what kind of powers they are,

164
00:12:53.430 --> 00:12:57.130
it's not like you have a
chance to win! How insolent!

165
00:12:57.130 --> 00:13:00.000
So that was right on the mark.
Now I kinda feel guilty.

166
00:13:01.040 --> 00:13:04.130
You're right. My specialty is cleanliness.

167
00:13:04.510 --> 00:13:07.070
I ate the Bubble Bubble Fruit...

168
00:13:07.070 --> 00:13:09.850
and became a soap human
whose entire body lathers.

169
00:13:13.400 --> 00:13:14.770
Isn't it wonderful?

170
00:13:14.770 --> 00:13:18.560
Whoa! How sexy! To be honest,
I'd be happy to have a secretary like her.

171
00:13:18.560 --> 00:13:20.230
Hey! What am I, a middle-aged guy?!

172
00:13:20.730 --> 00:13:25.570
But isn't that ineffective for fighting?
It doesn't look very strong.

173
00:13:25.570 --> 00:13:31.660
But I can freely manipulate the
bubbles that come out of my body.

174
00:13:34.620 --> 00:13:36.190
What? What's going on?

175
00:13:36.190 --> 00:13:37.680
I'll show you.

176
00:13:38.600 --> 00:13:40.040
The bubbles from the bathtub are...!

177
00:13:40.540 --> 00:13:42.420
Bubble Master:

178
00:13:42.740 --> 00:13:44.460
Soap Sheep!

179
00:13:48.330 --> 00:13:49.590
This is...

180
00:13:51.290 --> 00:13:52.920
How's this? Isn't it wonderful?

181
00:13:54.510 --> 00:13:56.270
You're an idiot, aren't you?

182
00:13:57.130 --> 00:13:59.270
You shouldn't be deceived by my appearance.

183
00:13:59.270 --> 00:14:00.280
What?

184
00:14:00.580 --> 00:14:03.480
Sheep Cloud: Relaxing Bubbles!

185
00:14:04.570 --> 00:14:09.490
You lost your strength at the
room's entrance. Why was that?

186
00:14:10.190 --> 00:14:11.250
That's right!

187
00:14:11.250 --> 00:14:14.090
That must've been her powers, too.

188
00:14:14.090 --> 00:14:15.210
Bubbles!

189
00:14:15.210 --> 00:14:18.230
Come to think of it, when I
stepped into this room,

190
00:14:21.830 --> 00:14:23.840
there were bubbles all over the floor!

191
00:14:26.130 --> 00:14:27.230
Shoot!

192
00:14:33.680 --> 00:14:35.430
You noticed it too late.

193
00:14:38.390 --> 00:14:40.310
My strength is fading away.

194
00:14:40.310 --> 00:14:44.900
This happened earlier, too, because I
stepped on the bubbles on the floor.

195
00:14:45.600 --> 00:14:49.760
You'll learn the horror of
this power little by little.

196
00:14:59.870 --> 00:15:04.460
The bubbles from my body scrub away all sorts of things.

197
00:15:04.780 --> 00:15:09.110
They naturally handle filth and spots, but they also sap your strength, among other things.

198
00:15:09.930 --> 00:15:16.390
And I don't want you to forget that I'm
an assassin from a secret organization.

199
00:15:18.830 --> 00:15:22.430
I can move my body! Her kicking
me made the bubbles go away!

200
00:15:23.360 --> 00:15:25.360
I'm not gonna take this anymore!

201
00:15:25.360 --> 00:15:27.530
Thunder Ball!

202
00:15:30.040 --> 00:15:31.520
That weapon's power alone...

203
00:15:32.370 --> 00:15:33.770
is still an unknown quantity to me.

204
00:15:36.580 --> 00:15:39.290
Golden Bubbles!

205
00:15:43.750 --> 00:15:45.160
What're you doing?!

206
00:15:48.330 --> 00:15:50.680
I can't stand!

207
00:15:50.680 --> 00:15:53.450
What?! What's wrong with my legs?!

208
00:15:56.800 --> 00:15:58.180
Pretty, aren't they?

209
00:15:58.180 --> 00:16:03.310
Everything I touch gains a beautiful gloss.

210
00:16:03.310 --> 00:16:06.230
I'll make your skin shiny...

211
00:16:06.930 --> 00:16:09.990
Every inch of your body.

212
00:16:20.580 --> 00:16:24.460
A man... A man...

213
00:16:24.800 --> 00:16:33.430
A man has battles that he must face head-on!

214
00:16:33.430 --> 00:16:34.880
Shave!

215
00:16:34.880 --> 00:16:37.730
Tempest Kick: Lotus!

216
00:16:41.590 --> 00:16:42.800
Take this!

217
00:16:42.800 --> 00:16:46.020
Song of the Willow!

218
00:17:32.130 --> 00:17:33.070
Iron Body!

219
00:17:57.420 --> 00:18:00.360
I don't know what's coming next,

220
00:18:00.360 --> 00:18:02.970
so I'm gonna go ahead
and replenish my cola first.

221
00:18:03.420 --> 00:18:06.680
Come to think of it, I wonder
how that deer's doing.

222
00:18:10.000 --> 00:18:12.360
What the heck's going on?!

223
00:18:23.700 --> 00:18:25.870
Wh-What the hell...

224
00:18:26.370 --> 00:18:27.720
is this?!

225
00:18:32.790 --> 00:18:36.550
That's the CP9 guy who was in the fridge!

226
00:18:36.550 --> 00:18:39.760
What?! Did this monster bring him down?!

227
00:18:48.390 --> 00:18:50.690
What the hell is this?

228
00:18:56.510 --> 00:19:00.070
I feel like that deer was
wearing the same kind of hat.

229
00:19:00.460 --> 00:19:04.420
Hey! You're not that deer-gorilla, are you?!

230
00:19:18.810 --> 00:19:21.260
Hey! This can't be happening!

231
00:19:21.740 --> 00:19:24.050
There's no mistake.

232
00:19:25.250 --> 00:19:27.020
Kumadori-san!

233
00:19:27.020 --> 00:19:30.160
He flew from the Tower of Justice?!

234
00:19:30.160 --> 00:19:33.100
It can't be! Who on earth could...?

235
00:19:35.110 --> 00:19:39.070
Good grief! What the hell is he?!

236
00:19:53.330 --> 00:19:54.580
A voice?

237
00:19:59.120 --> 00:20:00.180
Hm?

238
00:20:00.180 --> 00:20:01.710
Hey, hurry up!

239
00:20:01.710 --> 00:20:05.470
Why are you stopping, Nico Robin?!

240
00:20:06.000 --> 00:20:10.580
Hey, are you listening, Ms. My-existence-is-a-crime?!

241
00:20:10.580 --> 00:20:13.030
Hey, Lucci! Drag her along!

242
00:20:13.030 --> 00:20:15.150
Grab her by her hair!

243
00:20:19.270 --> 00:20:20.440
It's an order.

244
00:20:20.440 --> 00:20:23.100
Get moving, Nico Robin.

245
00:20:26.030 --> 00:20:33.450
Don't tell me, you still think that the
Straw Hats are coming to your rescue?

246
00:20:34.660 --> 00:20:36.120
How stupid!

247
00:20:36.120 --> 00:20:41.450
Are you seriously still laying your
hopes on such weak pirates?

248
00:20:41.450 --> 00:20:44.800
That explosion earlier was
surely just our imagination.

249
00:20:44.800 --> 00:20:47.180
There's no way that they can come here!

250
00:20:47.180 --> 00:20:53.020
While you're enjoying your little dream,
we'll pass through the Gates of Justice.

251
00:20:53.720 --> 00:20:58.250
The Bridge of Hesitation looms
in front of the Gates of Justice.

252
00:20:53.770 --> 00:21:02.740
<b>Underground Passage
(Current Location)</b>

253
00:20:57.560 --> 00:21:02.780
<b>"Bridge of Hesitation
(Halfway)"</b>

254
00:20:58.250 --> 00:21:01.080
We'll cross the first half of the bridge, which is now up.

255
00:21:01.080 --> 00:21:05.960
When the gates are opened,
the other half will rise from the sea,

256
00:21:02.740 --> 00:21:02.860
<b>Underground Passage
(Current Location)</b>

257
00:21:02.780 --> 00:21:09.490
<b>"Bridge of Hesitation
(Halfway)"</b>

258
00:21:05.970 --> 00:21:08.610
and we'll finally go through
the Gates of Justice.

259
00:21:06.070 --> 00:21:09.490
<b>"Gates of Justice
(Cross-Section)"</b>

260
00:21:09.490 --> 00:21:12.410
Once the gates are closed again,

261
00:21:12.410 --> 00:21:17.800
you'll never have the feeling of hope...

262
00:21:17.800 --> 00:21:20.450
ever again.

263
00:21:20.450 --> 00:21:25.050
The only feeling you'll have is a sense of guilt.

264
00:21:25.050 --> 00:21:30.850
You'll endlessly atone for your
sin of having lived until today.

265
00:21:30.850 --> 00:21:33.680
Right, Nico Robin?

266
00:21:48.700 --> 00:21:50.410
Now, let's hurry.

267
00:21:50.410 --> 00:21:52.270
Come on already!

268
00:21:57.930 --> 00:22:05.760
Robin!

269
00:22:13.450 --> 00:22:16.620
Wh-Wh-What was that?! I just heard a voice!

270
00:22:16.620 --> 00:22:18.640
Hey! What was that voice?!

271
00:22:21.520 --> 00:22:26.320
Chief, please take Nico Robin
and hurry on ahead.

272
00:22:28.080 --> 00:22:30.060
Hm? Doors?

273
00:22:30.860 --> 00:22:34.580
They don't look like iron this time.

274
00:22:45.640 --> 00:22:49.180
Hm? This room is bigger. Where am I?

275
00:22:51.770 --> 00:22:54.470
There you are! Pigeon guy!

276
00:22:57.430 --> 00:22:59.310
I'm glad you came.
